# Line endings — normalise in the repository, not on disk.
#
# Why this file exists: the repository was checked out with `core.autocrlf=true`
# on Windows, so every text file arrived CRLF while the committed blobs are LF.
# `git status` then reports 675 modified files that differ in nothing but their
# line endings, which makes an honest per-finding commit impossible: the real
# change is buried in the noise.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes the rule explicit and machine-checked rather than
# dependent on each contributor's local `core.autocrlf`. Files are stored LF in
# the repository; what a working copy looks like is then a checkout detail
# instead of a diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats: never touched, never diffed as text. Without these entries a
# normalisation pass would corrupt an image or a zip by rewriting byte sequences
# that happen to look like CRLF.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
